Let's craft each paragraph:
1. Bubble Sort: repeatedly swaps adjacent out-of-order elements; O(n^2) worst/avg, O(n) best with flag; use small nearly sorted arrays or teaching.
2. Selection Sort: finds min and swaps; O(n^2); use when writes expensive? small arrays.
3. Insertion Sort: builds sorted prefix by shifting; O(n^2), O(n) nearly sorted; use small or online sorting.
4. Merge Sort: divide conquer stable; O(n log n); use external sorting, stable sort.
5. Quick Sort: pivot partition; O(n log n) avg, O(n^2) worst; use in-memory sorting.
6. Heap Sort: max-heap extract; O(n log n); use guaranteed O(n log n) in-place.
7. Counting Sort: frequency counts; O(n+k); use integer keys bounded range.
8. Radix Sort: LSD/MSD digit passes; O(d(n+k)); use fixed-width integers/strings.
9. Bucket Sort: distribute into buckets; O(n) avg uniform, O(n^2) worst; use floating point uniform.
10. Binary Search: sorted array midpoint; O(log n); use sorted lookup.
11. Linear Search: scan; O(n); use unsorted or small.
12. Jump Search: sorted block jumps; O(sqrt n); use sorted arrays with expensive comparisons? maybe.
13. Exponential Search: doubling bounds then binary; O(log n); use unbounded/infinite sorted arrays.
14. Interpolation Search: estimate position; O(log log n) avg uniform, O(n) worst; use sorted uniform numeric data.
15. Dijkstra: nonnegative shortest paths; O((V+E) log V) binary heap; use road networks.
16. Bellman-Ford: relax edges V-1 times; O(VE); use negative weights and detect negative cycles.
17. Floyd-Warshall: all-pairs via intermediate vertices; O(V^3); use dense small graphs.
18. A*: f=g+h; worst exponential O(b^d), often O(E); use game AI/pathfinding with heuristic.
19. Kruskal
